The table structure information is (table names): 
['albums', 'sqlite_sequence', 'artists', 'customers', 'employees', 'genres', 'invoices', 'invoice_items', 'media_types', 'playlists', 'playlist_track', 'tracks', 'sqlite_stat1']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
artists.ArtistId: join‐key that identifies each artist  
artists.Name: used for alphabetical tie‑breaking and labeling results  
albums.AlbumId: join‐key that connects tracks to a specific album  
albums.ArtistId: links an album to its artist  
tracks.TrackId: join‐key that connects invoice_items to a specific track  
tracks.AlbumId: links a track to its album (hence to its artist)  
invoice_items.InvoiceId: joins invoice_items to invoices (to reach the customer)  
invoice_items.TrackId: joins invoice_items to tracks  
invoice_items.UnitPrice: price per track, needed for revenue (UnitPrice × Quantity)  
invoice_items.Quantity: number of items sold, multiply by UnitPrice for revenue  
invoices.InvoiceId: primary key to reach invoice_items and to reach the customer  
invoices.CustomerId: links each invoice to the purchasing customer  
customers.CustomerId: identifies the customer; used for grouping and averaging  

Primary conditions / filters that may be useful  
• To compute sales, use SUM(invoice_items.UnitPrice * invoice_items.Quantity)  
• When two artists tie on total sales, order by artists.Name ASC to break the tie  
• A “sale” exists only if an artist appears in invoice_items via the joins; artists without any sale will have NULL/0 totals (decide whether to include or exclude them)  
• When computing customer spending for the “top” and “bottom” artist, include only the invoice_items that belong to those artists  

Below are ten exploratory → increasingly complex queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress toward the final calculation.  

```sql
-- 1. Description: Quick look at the first 20 artist names.
SELECT DISTINCT "Name"
FROM "artists"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect some album‑to‑artist relationships.
SELECT a."AlbumId",
       a."Title",
       a."ArtistId",
       ar."Name" AS "ArtistName"
FROM "albums" AS a
JOIN "artists" AS ar ON a."ArtistId" = ar."ArtistId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Peek at how tracks connect to albums and artists.
SELECT t."TrackId",
       t."Name"            AS "TrackName",
       t."AlbumId",
       al."Title"          AS "AlbumTitle",
       al."ArtistId",
       ar."Name"           AS "ArtistName"
FROM   "tracks"  AS t
JOIN   "albums"  AS al ON t."AlbumId"  = al."AlbumId"
JOIN   "artists" AS ar ON al."ArtistId" = ar."ArtistId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Examine a handful of invoice items with pricing.
SELECT ii."InvoiceLineId",
       ii."InvoiceId",
       ii."TrackId",
       ii."UnitPrice",
       ii."Quantity"
FROM   "invoice_items" AS ii
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Calculate total revenue per artist (limited preview).
SELECT ar."ArtistId",
       ar."Name",
       SUM(ii."UnitPrice" * ii."Quantity") AS "ArtistRevenue"
FROM         "invoice_items" AS ii
JOIN         "tracks"        AS t  ON ii."TrackId" = t."TrackId"
JOIN         "albums"        AS al ON t."AlbumId"  = al."AlbumId"
JOIN         "artists"       AS ar ON al."ArtistId" = ar."ArtistId"
GROUP BY     ar."ArtistId", ar."Name"
ORDER BY     "ArtistRevenue" DESC, ar."Name" ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Identify the single highest‑revenue artist.
SELECT ar."ArtistId",
       ar."Name",
       SUM(ii."UnitPrice" * ii."Quantity") AS "TotalRevenue"
FROM   "invoice_items" AS ii
JOIN   "tracks"        AS t  ON ii."TrackId" = t."TrackId"
JOIN   "albums"        AS al ON t."AlbumId"  = al."AlbumId"
JOIN   "artists"       AS ar ON al."ArtistId" = ar."ArtistId"
GROUP BY ar."ArtistId", ar."Name"
ORDER BY "TotalRevenue" DESC, ar."Name" ASC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Identify the single lowest‑revenue artist (excluding NULL/0).
SELECT ar."ArtistId",
       ar."Name",
       SUM(ii."UnitPrice" * ii."Quantity") AS "TotalRevenue"
FROM   "invoice_items" AS ii
JOIN   "tracks"        AS t  ON ii."TrackId" = t."TrackId"
JOIN   "albums"        AS al ON t."AlbumId"  = al."AlbumId"
JOIN   "artists"       AS ar ON al."ArtistId" = ar."ArtistId"
GROUP BY ar."ArtistId", ar."Name"
HAVING "TotalRevenue" > 0
ORDER BY "TotalRevenue" ASC, ar."Name" ASC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Customer spending on the top‑selling artist.
WITH top_artist AS (
    SELECT ar."ArtistId"
    FROM   "invoice_items" AS ii
    JOIN   "tracks"        AS t  ON ii."TrackId" = t."TrackId"
    JOIN   "albums"        AS al ON t."AlbumId"  = al."AlbumId"
    JOIN   "artists"       AS ar ON al."ArtistId" = ar."ArtistId"
    GROUP BY ar."ArtistId", ar."Name"
    ORDER BY SUM(ii."UnitPrice" * ii."Quantity") DESC, ar."Name" ASC
    LIMIT 1
)
SELECT inv."CustomerId",
       SUM(ii."UnitPrice" * ii."Quantity") AS "SpendOnTopArtist"
FROM   top_artist         AS ta
JOIN   "tracks"           AS t   ON t."AlbumId" IN (SELECT "AlbumId" FROM "albums" WHERE "ArtistId" = ta."ArtistId")
JOIN   "invoice_items"    AS ii  ON ii."TrackId" = t."TrackId"
JOIN   "invoices"         AS inv ON inv."InvoiceId" = ii."InvoiceId"
GROUP BY inv."CustomerId"
ORDER BY inv."CustomerId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Customer spending on the lowest‑selling artist (non‑zero revenue).
WITH low_artist AS (
    SELECT ar."ArtistId"
    FROM   "invoice_items" AS ii
    JOIN   "tracks"        AS t  ON ii."TrackId" = t."TrackId"
    JOIN   "albums"        AS al ON t."AlbumId"  = al."AlbumId"
    JOIN   "artists"       AS ar ON al."ArtistId" = ar."ArtistId"
    GROUP BY ar."ArtistId", ar."Name"
    HAVING SUM(ii."UnitPrice" * ii."Quantity") > 0
    ORDER BY SUM(ii."UnitPrice" * ii."Quantity") ASC, ar."Name" ASC
    LIMIT 1
)
SELECT inv."CustomerId",
       SUM(ii."UnitPrice" * ii."Quantity") AS "SpendOnLowArtist"
FROM   low_artist          AS la
JOIN   "tracks"            AS t   ON t."AlbumId" IN (SELECT "AlbumId" FROM "albums" WHERE "ArtistId" = la."ArtistId")
JOIN   "invoice_items"     AS ii  ON ii."TrackId" = t."TrackId"
JOIN   "invoices"          AS inv ON inv."InvoiceId" = ii."InvoiceId"
GROUP BY inv."CustomerId"
ORDER BY inv."CustomerId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
